Role Overview

We are looking for an experienced Go (Golang) Developer with deep expertise in Kubernetes internal architecture to build, scale, and maintain custom Kubernetes Operators and Controllers. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

In this role, you will design Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs) and write reconciliation loops that automate the lifecycle management (provisioning, scaling, auto-healing, upgrades, and backup/restore) of complex distributed systems on cloud-native platforms. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities

&nbsp; Operator & Controller Development: Design, build, and maintain custom Kubernetes Operators using Go, controller-runtime, client-go, and Operator SDK / KubeBuilder frameworks. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

&nbsp; CRD Schema Design: Define clean, forward-compatible Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs) and OpenAPI v3 validation schemas tailored to complex application lifecycles. 

&nbsp; Reconciliation Logic: Implement idempotent, thread-safe reconciliation loops handling edge-triggered and level-triggered cluster events. 

&nbsp; System Integration: Integrate custom controllers with cloud APIs (AWS, GCP, Azure), service meshes (Istio/Linkerd), and GitOps pipelines (Argo CD, Flux). 

&nbsp; Testing & Quality Assurance: Write unit, integration, and end-to-end tests for operators using tools like envtest, kuttl, or standard Go testing packages. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

&nbsp; Observability & Health: Expose custom Prometheus metrics, trace reconciliation workflows, and generate Kubernetes events for auditability. 

Technical Qualifications

Must-Have Skills

&nbsp; Golang Proficiency: 3+ years of professional Go development experience with strong knowledge of concurrency patterns (goroutines, channels, context management), interfaces, and memory management. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

&nbsp; Kubernetes Internals: Strong understanding of Kubernetes control plane architecture (API Server, etcd, controller-manager, scheduler, informers, workqueues, and watch mechanics). &nbsp; &nbsp; 

&nbsp; Operator Frameworks: Hands-on experience with controller-runtime, KubeBuilder, or Operator SDK. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

&nbsp; Containerization & CI/CD: Proficient with Docker, Containerd, Helm charts, and building automated CI/CD pipelines for Go binaries and container images. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

- &nbsp; Testing: Experience writing unit tests, table-driven tests, and integration tests for Kubernetes custom controllers.

